      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Upon reviewing the patents provided, the most significant issue is the \"Layered Carbon-Ceramic Composite for Heat Dissipation in Electronic Components\" (US Patent 10,555,889), which appears to have a technology that closely resembles the proposed SSTM technology. This poses a challenge for your patent claim uniqueness since this patent may be considered prior art in the domain of using multi-layered graphene and ceramic structures for thermal management in electronics. Establishing the novelty may require demonstrating that your module incorporates a unique feature or an unexpectedly high level of efficiency that the existing patent does not cover. For investors, it's crucial to address this concern by outlining how the SSTM technology advances beyond the existing patent.",
